o why failures happen. You can't systematically improve because you're flying blind.\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.h2,{children:\"RAG 101: What You Actually Need to Know\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.pre,{children:(0,n.jsx)(e.code,{className:\"language-mermaid\",children:`graph LR\\r\n\tQ[User Query] --> E[Embedding Model]\\r\n\tE --> V[Vector Search]\\r\n\tV --> D[Retrieved Docs]\\r\n\tD --> P[Prompt + Context]\\r\n\tP --> L[LLM]\\r\n\tL --> A[Answer]\n`})}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.p,{children:\"The three failure modes of RAG systems are:\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsxs)(e.ol,{children:[`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Retrieval failure - wrong docs retrieved\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Context failure - right docs, bad ranking\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Generation failure - the LLM ignores the context\"}),`\n`]}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.p,{children:\"You can't fix what you can't see. Traditional logging shows inputs and outputs. LangSmith shows the entire pipeline, every step, every decision, every failure point.\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.h2,{children:\"The Observability Problem\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.pre,{children:(0,n.jsx)(e.code,{className:\"language-python\",children:`def rag_query(question: str) -> str:\\r\n\tdocs = retriever.get_relevant_docs(question)\\r\n\tanswer = llm.generate(question, docs)\\r\n\treturn answer  # Why did it fail?\n`})}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.p,{children:\"What you can't see:\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsxs)(e.ul,{children:[`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Which embedding model was actually used\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"What similarity scores were returned for each doc\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Which chunks were retrieved vs ignored\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"How the prompt was constructed before sending to the LLM\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Token usage and latency per step\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Why the model hallucinated instead of using the context\"}),`\n`]}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.h2,{children:\"Why LangSmith?\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.p,{children:\"Basic logging is not enough. LangSmith gives trace-level observability, systematic evaluation, and a way to optimize the pipeline with real data instead of guesswork.\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.pre,{children:(0,n.jsx)(e.code,{className:\"language-python\",children:`import logging\\r\n\\r\nlogging.info(f\"Query: {question}\")\\r\nlogging.info(f\"Retrieved docs: {len(docs)}\")\\r\nlogging.info(f\"Answer: {answer}\")\\r\nlogging.info(f\"Latency: {latency}ms\")\n`})}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.h2,{children:\"LangSmith Architecture\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.pre,{children:(0,n.jsx)(e.code,{className:\"language-mermaid\",children:`graph TB\\r\n\tsubgraph \"Your Application\"\\r\n\t\tApp[RAG Pipeline]\\r\n\t\tTrace[\"@traceable decorator\"]\\r\n\t\tApp --> Trace\\r\n\tend\\r\n\\r\n\tsubgraph \"LangSmith Backend\"\\r\n\t\tCollector[Trace Collector]\\r\n\t\tStore[Trace Storage]\\r\n\t\tUI[LangSmith Dashboard]\\r\n\t\tCollector --> Store\\r\n\t\tStore --> UI\\r\n\tend\\r\n\\r\n\tTrace -.->|async, non-blocking| Collector\n`})}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.p,{children:\"Key insight: LangSmith runs async, so tracing adds essentially no latency to your production app.\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.h2,{children:\"Setting Up Tracing\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.pre,{children:(0,n.jsx)(e.code,{className:\"language-python\",children:`import os\\r\nos.environ[\"LANGCHAIN_TRACING_V2\"] = \"true\"\\r\nos.environ[\"LANGCHAIN_API_KEY\"] = \"lsv2_pt_...\"\\r\nos.environ[\"LANGCHAIN_PROJECT\"] = \"rag-production\"\n`})}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.pre,{children:(0,n.jsx)(e.code,{className:\"language-python\",children:`from langsmith import traceable\\r\nfrom langchain_openai import ChatOpenAI, OpenAIEmbeddings\\r\nfrom langchain_community.vectorstores import FAISS\\r\n\\r\n@traceable\\r\ndef rag_query(question: str) -> dict:\\r\n\tembeddings = OpenAIEmbeddings()\\r\n\tvectorstore = FAISS.load_local(\"./db\", embeddings)\\r\n\tdocs = vectorstore.similarity_search(question, k=5)\\r\n\\r\n\tllm = ChatOpenAI(model=\"gpt-4\", temperature=0)\\r\n\tcontext = \"\\\\n\".join([d.page_content for d in docs])\\r\n\\r\n\tprompt = f\"\"\"Answer based on context only.\\r\n\\r\nContext: {context}\\r\n\\r\nQuestion: {question}\"\"\"\\r\n\\r\n\tanswer = llm.invoke(prompt)\\r\n\\r\n\treturn {\\r\n\t\t\"answer\": answer.content,\\r\n\t\t\"sources\": [d.metadata for d in docs]\\r\n\t}\n`})}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.h2,{children:\"Understanding Traces\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.pre,{children:(0,n.jsx)(e.code,{className:\"language-text\",children:`Trace: rag_query\\r\n\\u251C\\u2500 Duration: 2,347ms\\r\n\\u251C\\u2500 Cost: $0.0234\\r\n\\u251C\\u2500 Status: Success\\r\n\\u2502\\r\n\\u251C\\u2500 [Step 1] OpenAIEmbeddings.embed_query\\r\n\\u251C\\u2500 [Step 2] FAISS.similarity_search\\r\n\\u2514\\u2500 [Step 3] ChatOpenAI.invoke\n`})}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.p,{children:\"What this reveals:\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsxs)(e.ul,{children:[`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Retrieval working when similarity scores are strong\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"The LLM got the right context\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Latency is visible per step\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Cost per query is measurable\"}),`\n`]}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.h2,{children:\"Building Evaluation Datasets\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.p,{children:\"Manual testing does not scale. You need a dataset of golden questions, edge cases, and production examples.\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.pre,{children:(0,n.jsx)(e.code,{className:\"language-python\",children:`from langsmith import Client\\r\n\\r\nclient = Client()\\r\n\\r\ndataset = client.create_dataset(\\r\n\tdataset_name=\"rag-refund-policy\",\\r\n\tdescription=\"Test cases for refund policy queries\"\\r\n)\n`})}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.p,{children:\"Dataset types:\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsxs)(e.ul,{children:[`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Golden set - core functionality\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Edge cases - ambiguous queries and rare scenarios\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)(e.li,{children:\"Production sample - representative real-world queries\"}),`\n`,(0,n.jsx)